    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (81.09) and **Yordan Alvarez** (80.06) anchoring the offensive production. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** is our premier play, benefiting from a high-efficiency matchup against Arrighetti (4.97 xERA) and a favorable stolen base environment; the opposing pitcher\u2019s slow delivery adds significant upside for a player whose sprint speed is the engine of our category strategy. Meanwhile, **Yordan Alvarez** remains a must-start despite the \"Wind In\" factor, as his elite 0.421 xwOBA and platoon advantage against Taillon provide a high floor that mitigates any atmospheric drag. We are also looking for significant output from **Junior Caminero** (69.35), whose profile remains strong even against a high-caliber arm like Cole, provided he maintains his spot in the #2 hole.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Chase Meidroth**, who finished just outside the starting threshold with a 39.04 score. While he held a marginal case, the combination of a tough matchup against McDonald (2.94 xERA) and the uncertainty of a pending lineup forced us to prioritize the stability of **Hyeseong Kim** and **Caleb Durbin**, despite their lower raw scores. We must remain vigilant regarding **Casey Schmitt**; while his 57.89 score suggests a solid outing, we are banking on his assumed #3 slot in the lineup. Note that while **Christian Yelich** offers a decent floor, his platoon disadvantage against Wrobleski and the \"Wind In\" risk make him one of our more volatile starts today. We have confirmed that **Colt Keith**, **Zac Veen**, and **Lars Nootbaar** remain unavailable, keeping our bench rotation thin as we monitor weather-related risks for **Trea Turner** and **Kyle Schwarber**, both of whom see slight downgrades due to the current wind conditions.",
